  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA multiprofile PCA with avgpool is the best configuration (accuracy 0.5907, F1 0.5727), outperforming singleprofile RNA and transformer aggregation, while image-only ResNet50 singleprofile is weak. The main uncertainty is whether image features can add value on top of the strongest RNA baseline. config_018 keeps the best RNA profile and aggregation setting and adds ResNet50 image features with simple concat fusion, directly testing the marginal benefit of multimodality under the strongest known RNA configuration. This is the best use of the next experiment because it exploits the strongest evidence, uses a simple fusion baseline to avoid confounding complexity, and will clarify whether further multimodal exploration is worthwhile."
